import IUT.Applications.ABCSpecialization

/-!
# Points of bounded degree on the line minus three points

Source: Mochizuki, *Inter-universal Teichmüller Theory IV*, Theorem A and the sentence after it
(page 3), the notation recalled before Corollary 2.2 (page 40), Corollary 2.2 (pages 41 to 43,
read for the setting, condition (C2) and part (iii)), Corollary 2.3 with its proof (pages 54 and 55) and Remark 2.3.1 (pages 55 and
56). Second source: Mochizuki, *Arithmetic Elliptic Curves in General Position* ([GenEll]),
§1 (arithmetic divisors and normalized degree, page 4; Definition 1.2 and Example 1.3, pages 5
and 6; Proposition 1.4, page 6; Remark 1.4.1, Definition 1.5 and Remark 1.5.1, pages 8 and 9;
Propositions 1.6 and 1.7, page 9) and §2 (Theorem 2.1 and its proof, pages 11 to 13), with its
list of corrections, *Comments on "Arithmetic Elliptic Curves in General Position"* (July 2016,
pages 1 and 2).
Pages read for this file: IUT IV pages 3, 40 to 43 and 54 to 56; [GenEll] pages 4 to 6, 8, 9 and
11 to 13; the corrections, pages 1 and 2. Pages checked against rendered images: all of these.

**What this file is.** It defines, with Mathlib objects only, the three functions of [GenEll]
Definition 1.5 for the projective line `P = ℙ¹_ℚ` and the divisor `C = {0, 1, ∞}` at points of
`U_P(ℚ̄) = P(ℚ̄) \ C` over number fields: the normalized height `heightNF`, the normalized
log-different `logDiffNF` and the normalized log-conductor `logCondNF`. It states, as an open
proposition, the bounded degree inequality for these points
(`VojtaLineMinusThreePointsBoundedDegree`, with its fixed degree pieces
`VojtaLineMinusThreePointsDegreeAtMost d`). It proves that the degree one piece is equivalent to
`VojtaLineMinusThreePointsRational` of `IUT.Applications.ABCSpecialization`, hence to the abc
conjecture `Challenge.ABC`, so that the bounded degree statement implies `Challenge.ABC`. It
does not prove the bounded degree statement, and nothing here bears on whether the proofs in the
papers are correct.

**Which statements of the papers.** IUT IV, Corollary 2.3 (page 54): for a smooth, proper,
geometrically connected curve `X` over a number field, a reduced divisor `D ⊆ X` with
`U_X = X \ D` hyperbolic, a positive integer `d` and `ε > 0`, "one has an inequality of
'bounded discrepancy classes' `ht_{ω_X(D)} ≲ (1 + ε)(log-diff_X + log-cond_D)` of functions on
`U_X(ℚ̄)^{≤d}`, i.e., the function `(1 + ε)(log-diff_X + log-cond_D) - ht_{ω_X(D)}` is bounded
below by a constant on `U_X(ℚ̄)^{≤d}`". So the constant depends on `X`, `D`, `d` and `ε`, and on
nothing else. Its proof (pages 54 and 55) says that this "coincides precisely with the content
of [GenEll], Theorem 2.1, (i)". `VojtaLineMinusThreePointsBoundedDegree` is the instance
`X = ℙ¹_ℚ`, `D = {0, 1, ∞}` of that statement (here `ω_X(D) ≅ 𝒪(1)`, of degree `-2 + 3 = 1`),
that is, the instance `P`, `C` of [GenEll] Theorem 2.1 (i) (page 11), with the height
normalized as described below. It is not the corollary: all other curves are dropped. The
set `U_X(ℚ̄)^{≤d}` is the union of the `U_X(F)` over number fields `F` with `[F : ℚ] ≤ d`
([GenEll] Example 1.3 (i), page 5; IUT IV page 40); a point of it is recorded here as a pair
`(F, x)` where `F` is a number field, `x ∈ F \ {0, 1}`, and `F` is generated by `x`
(`ℚ⟮x⟯ = ⊤`), so that `F` is the minimal field of definition of the point in the sense of
[GenEll] Definition 1.5 (i) (page 8), which is the field at which Definition 1.5 (iii), (iv)
evaluate the log-different and the log-conductor. The bound `[F : ℚ] ≤ d` is then the degree
of the point. The quantifier `∀ F : Type` ranges over number fields in the lowest universe; every
number field has a copy there, so nothing is lost. Each point is represented by every pair
`(F, x)` isomorphic to it; the statement quantifies over all of them. The log-different and the
log-conductor are proved invariant under isomorphisms of pairs (`logCondNF_ringEquiv`, and
`NumberField.discr_eq_discr_of_ringEquiv` for the discriminant); for the height this invariance is
not formalized (Mathlib has no transport of its places along ring isomorphisms), but the height
of a rational number is computed in every number field (`heightNF_algebraMap_rat`).

**The relation `≲`.** `α ≲ β` means `α(x) - β(x) ≤ C` for a constant `C`: [GenEll]
Definition 1.2 (ii) (page 5) after correction (2), which reverses the printed direction, repeated
as IUT IV Remark 2.3.1 (ii) (page 55).

**The three functions.** [GenEll] page 4 defines an arithmetic divisor on a number field `F` as
a finite sum `Σ c_v v` over the places of `F`, the degree `deg_F` sending a finite place `v` to
`log(q_v)` (`q_v` the cardinality of the residue field) and an archimedean place to `1`, and the
normalized degree `(1 / [F : ℚ]) deg_F`, which is invariant under finite extension of `F`.

* Height. `ht_𝓜(x)` is the normalized degree of the pullback of an arithmetic line bundle on a
  model (page 4); its bounded discrepancy class depends only on the line bundle on `X_ℚ`
  (Proposition 1.4 (iii), page 6; Remark 1.4.1, page 8). Here `heightNF F x` is Mathlib's
  `Height.logHeight₁ x` divided by `[F : ℚ]`. Mathlib's `Height.logHeight₁` on a number field
  (`NumberField.logHeight₁_eq`) is the unnormalized sum
  `Σ_{v infinite} mult(v) log⁺ |x|_v + Σ_{v finite} log⁺ |x|_v`, where the finite places carry
  the absolute value `|x|_v = N(𝔭)^{-v_𝔭(x)}`; so it is `[F : ℚ]` times the absolute logarithmic
  Weil height. Mathlib also defines `NumberField.absLogHeight₁` (through `ℚ⟮x⟯` and the exponent
  `1 / [ℚ⟮x⟯ : ℚ]`) but proves nothing about it, and it has no lemma on invariance of heights
  under field extension. This file proves `heightNF_algebraMap_rat`: for every number field `F`
  and rational `q`, `heightNF F q = Height.logHeight₁ q = log max(|num q|, den q)`. As in
  `IUT.Applications.ABCSpecialization`, the identification of the height attached to
  `ω_P(C) ≅ 𝒪(1)` with the Weil height up to a bounded function is a standard computation not
  contained in [GenEll] and not formalized here; since `≲` absorbs bounded functions it does not
  change the statement.
* Log-different (Definition 1.5 (iii), page 8): "the different ideal of `F` determines an
  effective arithmetic divisor `δ_x ∈ ADiv(F)` which is supported in `V(F)^non`", and
  `log-diff_X(x) = deg_F(δ_x)` normalized. With the normalization of page 4 this is
  `(1 / [F : ℚ]) log N(𝔇_F)`, `𝔇_F` the different ideal of `𝓞_F` over `ℤ`, and by Mathlib's
  `NumberField.absNorm_differentIdeal` it equals `(1 / [F : ℚ]) log |disc F|`, with the absolute
  discriminant (`logDiffNF_eq`). It does not depend on `x` beyond `F = ℚ(x)`.
* Log-conductor (Definition 1.5 (iv), page 8, with correction (12): "conductor of `x` with
  respect to `D`"): pull `D` back along `Spec 𝓞_F → X` to the effective divisor `D_x`; the
  conductor is `(D_x)_red`, and `log-cond_D(x)` is its normalized degree. For the model `ℙ¹_ℤ`
  of `P` with `D` the closure of the sections `0`, `1`, `∞`, write `x` near a prime `𝔭` of
  `𝓞_F` as `(a : b)` with `a, b ∈ 𝓞_F` not both in `𝔭`; the section meets `0`, `∞`, `1` at `𝔭`
  exactly when `a`, `b`, `a - b` lies in `𝔭`. So `𝔭` lies in the support of `D_x` exactly when
  there are no `a, b ∈ 𝓞_F` with `a, b, a - b ∉ 𝔭` and `x b = a`; this is `MeetsBoundaryAt`, and
  `logCondNF F x = (1 / [F : ℚ]) Σ log q_𝔭` over these primes, each counted once, with `q_𝔭`
  the cardinality of `𝓞_F / 𝔭`. The pullback description is the definition; the theorem
  `meetsBoundaryAt_iff_valuation` proves that it is the set of primes with `v_𝔭(x) ≠ 0` or
  `v_𝔭(x - 1) ≠ 0` (equivalently, `v_𝔭(x) ≠ 0` or `v_𝔭(x - 1) > 0`, since `v_𝔭(x - 1) < 0`
  forces `v_𝔭(x) < 0`). Another model of `(P, C)` changes the log-conductor only at finitely
  many primes, hence by a bounded function (Remark 1.5.1, pages 8 and 9), which `≲` absorbs.

**Normalization checks.** At a rational point `q ∉ {0, 1}` the three functions are
`log max(|num q|, den q)`, `0` and `log (ratConductor q)` (`heightNF_rat`, `logDiffNF_rat`,
`logCondNF_rat`): these are the functions of `VojtaLineMinusThreePointsRational`. At the point
`x = -ζ₃` (a primitive sixth root of unity) of the quadratic field `ℚ(ζ₃)`, which generates
it: the height is `0`, the log-different is `(1/2) log 3` (the discriminant is `-3`), and the
log-conductor is `0`, because `x` and `x - 1 = ζ₃²` are units. These are stated for every
number field `K` with `IsCyclotomicExtension {3} ℚ K`, and instantiated at Mathlib's
`CyclotomicField 3 ℚ` in `exists_point_cyclotomicFieldThree` (instance search does not find
that instance here, so the proof supplies `CyclotomicField.isCyclotomicExtension` by name).

**The compactly bounded form is stated elsewhere.** [GenEll] Theorem 2.1 (ii) (page 11) asserts the
same inequality on `K_V ∩ U_P(ℚ̄)^{≤d}` for every compactly bounded subset `K_V ⊆ U_P(ℚ̄)` whose
support contains a fixed finite set `Σ` of primes; IUT IV takes `Σ = {2}` and adds the
condition `(*_{j-inv})` (pages 41 and 55). By Example 1.3 (ii) (pages 5 and 6) with corrections
(8), (9) and Remark 2.3.1 (vi) (page 56), `K_V` is given by a finite set `V` of places of `ℚ`
containing the archimedean one and, for `v ∈ V`, a nonempty compact domain `K_v` of `U(ℂ)`
stable under complex conjugation (archimedean `v`), or a nonempty `Gal(ℚ̄_v / ℚ_v)`-stable subset
`K_v ⊆ U(ℚ̄_v)` whose intersection with `X(K)` is a compact domain for every finite extension
`K ⊆ ℚ̄_v` of `ℚ_v` (finite `v`); `x ∈ X(F)` lies in `K_V` when for each `v ∈ V` the `[F : ℚ]`
points of `X(ℂ)`, respectively `X(ℚ̄_v)`, determined by `x` lie in `K_v`. These are points of
`ℚ̄_v`, not of the completions of `F`. Mathlib has `ℚ̄_p` (`PadicAlgCl p`) with its norm, and ring
homomorphisms from `F` into it; a faithful definition would quantify over the finite
intermediate extensions of `PadicAlgCl p / ℚ_[p]` with their subspace topologies and over the
`ℚ_[p]`-automorphisms of `PadicAlgCl p`. This file does not build that definition;
`IUT/Applications/CompactlyBounded.lean` does, states form (ii) as `genEllTheorem2_1iiStatement`,
and proves that it follows from `VojtaLineMinusThreePointsBoundedDegree` by restriction (proof of
Theorem 2.1: "The fact that (i) ⟹ (ii) is immediate from the definitions"). That form (ii)
implies `Challenge.ABC` is not shown.

**Open items between IUT IV and `VojtaLineMinusThreePointsBoundedDegree`.** None of these is
formalized.
1. IUT IV Theorem 1.10, applied to the initial Θ-data built in Corollary 2.2.
2. IUT IV Corollary 2.2 (pages 41 to 43): for compactly bounded `K_V` whose support contains `2`
   and which satisfies `(*_{j-inv})`, (i) an equality of bounded discrepancy classes
   `(1/6) log(𝔮^∀) ≈ ht_{ω_X(D)}` on `K_V`, (ii) condition (C2) bounding `(1/6) log(𝔮^∀)` by
   `(1 + ε_E)(log-diff_X(x_E) + log-cond_D(x_E)) + C_K` outside a finite set, (iii) the bound
   `ε_E ≤ ε` outside a finite set. With them the proof of Corollary 2.3 (page 55) derives form
   (ii) of [GenEll] Theorem 2.1 for `Σ = {2}`, noting that `(*_{j-inv})` is vacuous for fixed
   `d`.
3. The passage (ii) ⟹ (i) of [GenEll] Theorem 2.1 (pages 11 to 13): a connected finite étale
   Galois covering `U_Y → U_X` with ramification index `e` over `D`, which raises the degree
   bound to `d' = d deg(Y/X)`; the reduction to `D = ∅`; the compactness argument at the places
   of `V`; the noncritical Belyi map `φ : X → P` of an earlier paper of Mochizuki (cited as
   [Mzk1] Theorem 2.5), unramified over `U_P` and noncritical at the limit points; Propositions
   1.4, 1.6 and 1.7; and correction (5) to the last display. Even for `X = P` and `d = 1` this
   route uses form (ii) at the degree `d' > 1`.
4. The identification of `ht_{ω_P(C)}` with the Weil height up to a bounded function (above).

**Main results.**

* `meetsBoundaryAt_iff_valuation`: the pullback description of the conductor is the valuation
  description.
* `logDiffNF_eq`, `heightNF_nonneg`, `logDiffNF_nonneg`, `logCondNF_nonneg`.
* `logCondNF_one_sub`, `logCondNF_inv`, `heightNF_inv`, `abs_heightNF_one_sub_sub_le`,
  `adjoin_one_sub_eq_top_iff`, `adjoin_inv_eq_top_iff`: behavior under `x ↦ 1 - x` and
  `x ↦ 1 / x`, which generate the six permutations of `{0, 1, ∞}`.
* `heightNF_algebraMap_rat`, `heightNF_rat`, `logDiffNF_rat`, `logCondNF_rat`: the values at
  rational points.
* `logCondNF_ringEquiv`: invariance of the log-conductor under isomorphisms of number fields.
* `degreeAtMostOne_iff_rational`, `degreeAtMostOne_iff_ABC`, `degreeAtMost_mono`,
  `abc_of_degreeAtMost`, `abc_of_boundedDegree`.
* `heightNF_sixthRoot`, `logDiffNF_cyclotomicThree`, `logCondNF_sixthRoot`,
  `adjoin_sixthRoot_eq_top`, `exists_point_cyclotomicFieldThree`: the example in `ℚ(ζ₃)`.
-/

namespace IUT.VojtaNumberField

open NumberField IsDedekindDomain
open IUT.ABCSpecialization

/-! ## Definitions -/

section Definitions

variable (K : Type*) [Field K] [NumberField K]

/-- The point `y` of `ℙ¹(K)` reduces at the prime `v` of `𝓞_K` to a point of `ℙ¹ \ {0, 1, ∞}`:
there are `a, b ∈ 𝓞_K` with `y b = a` and none of `a`, `b`, `a - b` in `v`, that is, `y = (a : b)`
near `v` with the coordinates of the three points `0`, `∞`, `1` all nonzero modulo `v`. -/
def ReducesAwayFromBoundary (v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)) (y : K) : Prop :=
  ∃ a b : 𝓞 K, a ∉ v.asIdeal ∧ b ∉ v.asIdeal ∧ a - b ∉ v.asIdeal ∧
    y * algebraMap (𝓞 K) K b = algebraMap (𝓞 K) K a

/-- The prime `v` of `𝓞_K` lies in the support of the pullback of `D = {0, 1, ∞}` along the
section `Spec 𝓞_K → ℙ¹_ℤ` defined by `y` ([GenEll] Definition 1.5 (iv), page 8): the point `y`
reduces modulo `v` to `0`, `1` or `∞`. -/
def MeetsBoundaryAt (v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)) (y : K) : Prop :=
  ¬ ReducesAwayFromBoundary K v y

/-- The normalized logarithmic height of `y ∈ K`: Mathlib's `Height.logHeight₁ y`, which on a
number field is `Σ_{v infinite} mult(v) log⁺ |y|_v + Σ_{v finite} log⁺ |y|_v`, divided by
`[K : ℚ]` (the normalized degree of [GenEll] page 4). -/
noncomputable def heightNF (y : K) : ℝ :=
  Height.logHeight₁ y / Module.finrank ℚ K

/-- The normalized log-different of `K` ([GenEll] Definition 1.5 (iii), page 8, for a point
whose minimal field of definition is `K`): `(1 / [K : ℚ]) log N(𝔇_K)`, with `𝔇_K` the different
ideal of `𝓞_K` over `ℤ`. It equals `(1 / [K : ℚ]) log |disc K|` (`logDiffNF_eq`). -/
noncomputable def logDiffNF : ℝ :=
  Real.log (Ideal.absNorm (differentIdeal ℤ (𝓞 K))) / Module.finrank ℚ K

open Classical in
/-- The normalized log-conductor of `y ∈ K` with respect to `D = {0, 1, ∞}` ([GenEll]
Definition 1.5 (iv), page 8, with correction (12), for the model `ℙ¹_ℤ` with the three
sections): `(1 / [K : ℚ]) Σ log q_v` over the primes `v` of `𝓞_K` at which `y` meets `D`, each
counted once, where `q_v` is the cardinality of the residue field `𝓞_K / v`. -/
noncomputable def logCondNF (y : K) : ℝ :=
  (∑ᶠ v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K),
    if MeetsBoundaryAt K v y then Real.log (Nat.card (𝓞 K ⧸ v.asIdeal)) else 0) /
    Module.finrank ℚ K

end Definitions

/-! ## The statements -/

/-- **An open statement, not a theorem: the instance `X = ℙ¹_ℚ`, `D = {0, 1, ∞}` of the
conclusion of IUT IV, Corollary 2.3, for points of degree at most `d`.** For every `ε > 0` there
is a constant `C` such that for every number field `F` generated by a point `x ∈ F \ {0, 1}` with
`[F : ℚ] ≤ d`, `ht(x) ≤ (1 + ε)(log-diff(x) + log-cond(x)) + C`. Here `F` is the minimal field of
definition of the point ([GenEll] Definition 1.5 (i)), and the three functions are `heightNF`,
`logDiffNF` and `logCondNF`. The constant depends on `d` and `ε` only, as in Corollary 2.3
(page 54). This file proves that the case `d = 1` is equivalent to the abc conjecture
(`degreeAtMostOne_iff_ABC`). -/
def VojtaLineMinusThreePointsDegreeAtMost (d : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ ε : ℝ, 0 < ε → ∃ C : ℝ, ∀ (F : Type) [Field F] [NumberField F] (x : F),
    IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {x} = ⊤ → Module.finrank ℚ F ≤ d → x ≠ 0 → x ≠ 1 →
      heightNF F x ≤ (1 + ε) * (logDiffNF F + logCondNF F x) + C

/-- **An open statement, not a theorem: the instance `X = ℙ¹_ℚ`, `D = {0, 1, ∞}` of IUT IV,
Corollary 2.3, equivalently of [GenEll] Theorem 2.1 (i).** For every positive integer `d`, the
inequality `ht ≲ (1 + ε)(log-diff + log-cond)` holds on the points of `ℙ¹ \ {0, 1, ∞}` of degree
at most `d`, for every `ε > 0`. It implies the abc conjecture (`abc_of_boundedDegree`); the
converse is not proved here. -/
def VojtaLineMinusThreePointsBoundedDegree : Prop :=
  ∀ d : ℕ, 1 ≤ d → VojtaLineMinusThreePointsDegreeAtMost d

/-! ## Basic properties -/

section Basic

variable (K : Type*) [Field K] [NumberField K]

/-- The degree `[K : ℚ]` is positive. -/
theorem finrank_pos_real : (0 : ℝ) < Module.finrank ℚ K := by
  exact_mod_cast Module.finrank_pos

/-- The pullback description of the conductor is the valuation description: `y` meets
`{0, 1, ∞}` at `v` exactly when `v(y) ≠ 0` or `v(y - 1) ≠ 0` (additively), that is, when the
multiplicative `v`-adic valuation of `y` or of `y - 1` is not `1`. -/
theorem meetsBoundaryAt_iff_valuation (v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)) (y : K) :
    MeetsBoundaryAt K v y ↔ v.valuation K y ≠ 1 ∨ v.valuation K (y - 1) ≠ 1 := by
  have key : ReducesAwayFromBoundary K v y ↔
      v.valuation K y = 1 ∧ v.valuation K (y - 1) = 1 := by
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨a, b, ha, hb, hab, h⟩
      have va := (HeightOneSpectrum.valuation_eq_one_iff_notMem (K := K) v).mpr ha
      have vb := (HeightOneSpectrum.valuation_eq_one_iff_notMem (K := K) v).mpr hb
      have vab := (HeightOneSpectrum.valuation_eq_one_iff_notMem (K := K) v).mpr hab
      refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
      · have := congrArg (v.valuation K) h
        rwa [map_mul, vb, mul_one, va] at this
      · have h' : (y - 1) * algebraMap (𝓞 K) K b = algebraMap (𝓞 K) K (a - b) := by
          rw [map_sub, ← h]; ring
        have := congrArg (v.valuation K) h'
        rwa [map_mul, vb, mul_one, vab] at this
    · rintro ⟨hy, hy1⟩
      obtain ⟨n, d, hnd⟩ := HeightOneSpectrum.exists_primeCompl_mul_eq_of_integer v y hy.le
      have hd : (d : 𝓞 K) ∉ v.asIdeal := d.prop
      have vd := (HeightOneSpectrum.valuation_eq_one_iff_notMem (K := K) v).mpr hd
      refine ⟨n, d, ?_, hd, ?_, hnd⟩
      · rw [← HeightOneSpectrum.valuation_eq_one_iff_notMem (K := K) v, ← hnd, map_mul, hy, vd,
          one_mul]
      · rw [← HeightOneSpectrum.valuation_eq_one_iff_notMem (K := K) v, map_sub, ← hnd,
          show y * algebraMap (𝓞 K) K d - algebraMap (𝓞 K) K d =
            (y - 1) * algebraMap (𝓞 K) K d by ring, map_mul, hy1, vd, one_mul]
  rw [MeetsBoundaryAt, key, not_and_or]

/-- The log-different is `(1 / [K : ℚ]) log |disc K|`, by Mathlib's
`NumberField.absNorm_differentIdeal`. -/
theorem logDiffNF_eq : logDiffNF K = Real.log |(discr K : ℝ)| / Module.finrank ℚ K := by
  rw [logDiffNF, absNorm_differentIdeal K (𝓞 K), Nat.cast_natAbs, Int.cast_abs]

/-- The normalized height is nonnegative. -/
theorem heightNF_nonneg (y : K) : 0 ≤ heightNF K y :=
  div_nonneg (Height.zero_le_logHeight₁ y) (Nat.cast_nonneg _)

/-- The log-different is nonnegative: the discriminant is a nonzero integer. -/
theorem logDiffNF_nonneg : 0 ≤ logDiffNF K := by
  rw [logDiffNF_eq]
  refine div_nonneg (Real.log_nonneg ?_) (Nat.cast_nonneg _)
  have h : (1 : ℤ) ≤ |discr K| := Int.one_le_abs (discr_ne_zero K)
  exact_mod_cast h

/-- The log-conductor is nonnegative. -/
theorem logCondNF_nonneg (y : K) : 0 ≤ logCondNF K y := by
  unfold logCondNF
  refine div_nonneg (finsum_nonneg fun v => ?_) (Nat.cast_nonneg _)
  split_ifs
  · exact Real.log_natCast_nonneg _
  · exact le_rfl

end Basic

/-! ## The six substitutions -/

section Symmetries

variable {K : Type*} [Field K] [NumberField K]

omit [NumberField K] in
/-- A local representation `y = (a : b)` gives the representation `1 - y = (b - a : b)`. -/
theorem reducesAwayFromBoundary_one_sub {v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)} {y : K}
    (h : ReducesAwayFromBoundary K v y) : ReducesAwayFromBoundary K v (1 - y) := by
  obtain ⟨a, b, ha, hb, hab, h⟩ := h
  refine ⟨b - a, b, ?_, hb, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rwa [← neg_sub, neg_mem_iff]
  · rwa [sub_sub_cancel_left, neg_mem_iff]
  · rw [map_sub, ← h]; ring

/-- A local representation `y = (a : b)` gives the representation `1 / y = (b : a)`. -/
theorem reducesAwayFromBoundary_inv {v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)} {y : K}
    (h : ReducesAwayFromBoundary K v y) : ReducesAwayFromBoundary K v y⁻¹ := by
  obtain ⟨a, b, ha, hb, hab, h⟩ := h
  have hy : y ≠ 0 := by
    rintro rfl
    apply ha
    have h0 : algebraMap (𝓞 K) K a = algebraMap (𝓞 K) K 0 := by rw [← h, zero_mul, map_zero]
    rw [IsFractionRing.injective (𝓞 K) K h0]
    exact zero_mem _
  refine ⟨b, a, hb, ha, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rwa [← neg_sub, neg_mem_iff]
  · rw [← h, ← mul_assoc, inv_mul_cancel₀ hy, one_mul]

omit [NumberField K] in
/-- The point `1 - y` meets `{0, 1, ∞}` at the same primes as `y` (`x ↦ 1 - x` exchanges `0`
and `1` and fixes `∞`). -/
theorem meetsBoundaryAt_one_sub_iff (v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)) (y : K) :
    MeetsBoundaryAt K v (1 - y) ↔ MeetsBoundaryAt K v y := by
  refine not_congr ⟨fun h => ?_, reducesAwayFromBoundary_one_sub⟩
  simpa using reducesAwayFromBoundary_one_sub h

/-- The point `1 / y` meets `{0, 1, ∞}` at the same primes as `y` (`x ↦ 1 / x` exchanges `0`
and `∞` and fixes `1`). -/
theorem meetsBoundaryAt_inv_iff (v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)) (y : K) :
    MeetsBoundaryAt K v y⁻¹ ↔ MeetsBoundaryAt K v y := by
  refine not_congr ⟨fun h => ?_, reducesAwayFromBoundary_inv⟩
  simpa using reducesAwayFromBoundary_inv h

open Classical in
/-- **The log-conductor is invariant under `x ↦ 1 - x`.** -/
theorem logCondNF_one_sub (y : K) : logCondNF K (1 - y) = logCondNF K y := by
  simp only [logCondNF, meetsBoundaryAt_one_sub_iff]

open Classical in
/-- **The log-conductor is invariant under `x ↦ 1 / x`.** -/
theorem logCondNF_inv (y : K) : logCondNF K y⁻¹ = logCondNF K y := by
  simp only [logCondNF, meetsBoundaryAt_inv_iff]

/-- **The height is invariant under `x ↦ 1 / x`** (Mathlib's `Height.logHeight₁_inv`). -/
theorem heightNF_inv (y : K) : heightNF K y⁻¹ = heightNF K y := by
  rw [heightNF, heightNF, Height.logHeight₁_inv]

/-- **The height changes by at most `log 2` under `x ↦ 1 - x`**, from Mathlib's
`Height.logHeight₁_sub_le` and the normalization by `[K : ℚ]`. -/
theorem abs_heightNF_one_sub_sub_le (y : K) :
    |heightNF K (1 - y) - heightNF K y| ≤ Real.log 2 := by
  have hn := finrank_pos_real K
  have hw : (Height.totalWeight K : ℝ) = Module.finrank ℚ K := by
    exact_mod_cast totalWeight_eq_finrank K
  have h1 := Height.logHeight₁_sub_le (1 : K) y
  have h2 := Height.logHeight₁_sub_le (1 : K) (1 - y)
  rw [sub_sub_cancel] at h2
  rw [Height.logHeight₁_one, hw] at h1 h2
  rw [heightNF, heightNF, ← sub_div, abs_div, abs_of_pos hn, div_le_iff₀ hn, abs_sub_le_iff]
  constructor <;> linarith

/-- `1 - y` generates the same field as `y`. -/
theorem adjoin_one_sub_eq_top_iff (y : K) :
    IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {1 - y} = ⊤ ↔ IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {y} = ⊤ := by
  have h1 : IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {y} ≤ IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {1 - y} :=
    IntermediateField.adjoin_simple_le_iff.mpr (by
      have := sub_mem (one_mem (IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {1 - y}))
        (IntermediateField.subset_adjoin ℚ {1 - y} (Set.mem_singleton _))
      rwa [sub_sub_cancel] at this)
  have h2 : IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {1 - y} ≤ IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {y} :=
    IntermediateField.adjoin_simple_le_iff.mpr
      (sub_mem (one_mem _) (IntermediateField.subset_adjoin ℚ {y} (Set.mem_singleton _)))
  rw [le_antisymm h2 h1]

/-- `1 / y` generates the same field as `y`. -/
theorem adjoin_inv_eq_top_iff (y : K) :
    IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {y⁻¹} = ⊤ ↔ IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {y} = ⊤ := by
  have h1 : IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {y} ≤ IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {y⁻¹} :=
    IntermediateField.adjoin_simple_le_iff.mpr (by
      simpa using inv_mem (IntermediateField.subset_adjoin ℚ {y⁻¹} (Set.mem_singleton _)))
  have h2 : IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {y⁻¹} ≤ IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {y} :=
    IntermediateField.adjoin_simple_le_iff.mpr
      (inv_mem (IntermediateField.subset_adjoin ℚ {y} (Set.mem_singleton _)))
  rw [le_antisymm h2 h1]

end Symmetries

/-! ## Heights of rational numbers in a number field -/

section RationalHeight

variable (K : Type*) [Field K] [NumberField K]

/-- A supremum over `Fin 2` is a maximum. -/
theorem iSup_finTwo_eq_max (f : Fin 2 → ℝ) : iSup f = max (f 0) (f 1) := by
  apply le_antisymm
  · exact ciSup_le fun i => by fin_cases i <;> simp
  · exact max_le (Finite.le_ciSup_of_le 0 le_rfl) (Finite.le_ciSup_of_le 1 le_rfl)

/-- For rational `q`, the multiplicative height of `q` in `K` is the `[K : ℚ]`-th power of its
height in `ℚ`: at each finite place the coprime numerator and denominator of `q` give the
maximum `1`, and at each infinite place the maximum is `max(|num q|, den q)`. -/
theorem mulHeight₁_algebraMap_rat (q : ℚ) :
    Height.mulHeight₁ (algebraMap ℚ K q) = Height.mulHeight₁ q ^ Module.finrank ℚ K := by
  have hq : algebraMap ℚ K q = (q.num : K) / (q.den : K) := by
    rw [eq_ratCast, Rat.cast_def]
  have hx : ![(q.num : K), (q.den : K)] ≠ 0 := by
    intro h
    have := congrFun h 1
    simp at this
  have hinf : ∀ v : InfinitePlace K, (⨆ i, v (![(q.num : K), (q.den : K)] i)) =
      ((max q.num.natAbs q.den : ℕ) : ℝ) := by
    intro v
    rw [iSup_finTwo_eq_max]
    simp [Int.norm_eq_abs, Nat.cast_natAbs]
  have hfin : ∀ v : FinitePlace K, (⨆ i, v (![(q.num : K), (q.den : K)] i)) = 1 := by
    intro v
    have hv : IsNonarchimedean (v ·) := FinitePlace.add_le v
    have H (n : ℤ) : v n ≤ 1 := hv.apply_intCast_le_one (map_zero_le v 1) (map_one v)
      (map_neg_eq_map v)
    have Hd : v (q.den : K) ≤ 1 := by exact_mod_cast H q.den
    rw [iSup_finTwo_eq_max]
    simp only [Matrix.cons_val_zero, Matrix.cons_val_one]
    refine le_antisymm (max_le (H _) Hd) ?_
    obtain ⟨u, w, huw⟩ := Rat.isCoprime_num_den q
    have h1 : (1 : K) = (u : K) * q.num + (w : K) * q.den := by exact_mod_cast huw.symm
    calc (1 : ℝ) = v ((u : K) * q.num + (w : K) * q.den) := by rw [← h1, map_one]
      _ ≤ max (v ((u : K) * q.num)) (v ((w : K) * q.den)) := FinitePlace.add_le v _ _
      _ ≤ max (v (q.num : K)) (v (q.den : K)) := by
        rw [map_mul, map_mul]
        exact max_le_max (mul_le_of_le_one_left (apply_nonneg v _) (H u))
          (mul_le_of_le_one_left (apply_nonneg v _) (H w))
  rw [hq, Height.mulHeight₁_div_eq_mulHeight, NumberField.mulHeight_eq hx, Rat.mulHeight₁_eq_max]
  simp_rw [hinf, hfin, finprod_one, mul_one, Finset.prod_pow_eq_pow_sum,
    InfinitePlace.sum_mult_eq]

/-- For rational `q`, `Height.logHeight₁ q` computed in `K` is `[K : ℚ]` times its value in
`ℚ`. -/
theorem logHeight₁_algebraMap_rat (q : ℚ) :
    Height.logHeight₁ (algebraMap ℚ K q) = Module.finrank ℚ K * Height.logHeight₁ q := by
  rw [Height.logHeight₁_eq_log_mulHeight₁, Height.logHeight₁_eq_log_mulHeight₁,
    mulHeight₁_algebraMap_rat, Real.log_pow]

/-- **The normalized height of a rational number does not depend on the number field**: it is
`Height.logHeight₁ q = log max(|num q|, den q)` in every number field. -/
theorem heightNF_algebraMap_rat (q : ℚ) :
    heightNF K (algebraMap ℚ K q) = Height.logHeight₁ q := by
  rw [heightNF, logHeight₁_algebraMap_rat, mul_div_cancel_left₀ _ (finrank_pos_real K).ne']

end RationalHeight

/-! ## Rational points -/

section Rational

/-- A natural number lies in the prime `v` of `𝓞_ℚ` exactly when the prime number generating
`v` divides it. -/
theorem natCast_mem_iff_natGenerator_dvd (v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 ℚ)) (k : ℕ) :
    (k : 𝓞 ℚ) ∈ v.asIdeal ↔ Rat.HeightOneSpectrum.natGenerator v ∣ k := by
  rw [Rat.HeightOneSpectrum.natGenerator_dvd_iff,
    ← map_natCast (Rat.IsIntegralClosure.intEquiv (𝓞 ℚ)) k, Ideal.apply_mem_of_equiv_iff]

/-- An integer lies in the prime `v` of `𝓞_ℚ` exactly when the prime number generating `v`
divides its absolute value. -/
theorem intCast_mem_iff_natGenerator_dvd (v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 ℚ)) (k : ℤ) :
    (k : 𝓞 ℚ) ∈ v.asIdeal ↔ Rat.HeightOneSpectrum.natGenerator v ∣ k.natAbs := by
  obtain ⟨n, rfl | rfl⟩ := Int.eq_nat_or_neg k
  · simp [natCast_mem_iff_natGenerator_dvd]
  · simp [natCast_mem_iff_natGenerator_dvd, neg_mem_iff]

/-- The residue field of `𝓞_ℚ` at `v` has as many elements as the prime number generating
`v`. -/
theorem card_quot_eq_natGenerator (v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 ℚ)) :
    Nat.card (𝓞 ℚ ⧸ v.asIdeal) = Rat.HeightOneSpectrum.natGenerator v := by
  set p := Rat.HeightOneSpectrum.natGenerator v
  rw [Nat.card_congr (Ideal.quotientEquiv v.asIdeal (Ideal.span {((p : ℕ) : ℤ)})
      (Rat.IsIntegralClosure.intEquiv (𝓞 ℚ))
      (by rw [Rat.HeightOneSpectrum.span_natGenerator]; rfl)).toEquiv,
    Nat.card_congr (Int.quotientSpanNatEquivZMod p).toEquiv, Nat.card_zmod]

/-- A rational number `q` meets `{0, 1, ∞}` at the prime `v` of `𝓞_ℚ` exactly when the prime
number `p` generating `v` divides `num q`, `num q - den q` (the numerator of `q - 1`) or
`den q`. -/
theorem meetsBoundaryAt_rat_iff (v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 ℚ)) (q : ℚ) :
    MeetsBoundaryAt ℚ v q ↔
      Rat.HeightOneSpectrum.natGenerator v ∣ q.num.natAbs * (q.num - q.den).natAbs * q.den := by
  have hp : (Rat.HeightOneSpectrum.natGenerator v).Prime :=
    Rat.HeightOneSpectrum.prime_natGenerator v
  have hcop : ¬ ((q.num : 𝓞 ℚ) ∈ v.asIdeal ∧ (q.den : 𝓞 ℚ) ∈ v.asIdeal) := by
    rintro ⟨h1, h2⟩
    rw [intCast_mem_iff_natGenerator_dvd] at h1
    rw [natCast_mem_iff_natGenerator_dvd] at h2
    have := Nat.dvd_gcd h1 h2
    rw [q.reduced.gcd_eq_one] at this
    exact hp.one_lt.ne' (Nat.dvd_one.mp this)
  have key : ReducesAwayFromBoundary ℚ v q ↔ ¬ ((q.num : 𝓞 ℚ) ∈ v.asIdeal ∨
      ((q.num - q.den : ℤ) : 𝓞 ℚ) ∈ v.asIdeal ∨ (q.den : 𝓞 ℚ) ∈ v.asIdeal) := by
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨a, b, ha, hb, hab, h⟩
      have hnb : (q.num : 𝓞 ℚ) * b = (q.den : 𝓞 ℚ) * a := by
        apply IsFractionRing.injective (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ
        rw [map_mul, map_mul, map_intCast, map_natCast, ← h, ← Rat.mul_den_eq_num]
        ring
      have hdab : ((q.num - q.den : ℤ) : 𝓞 ℚ) * b = (q.den : 𝓞 ℚ) * (a - b) := by
        push_cast
        rw [sub_mul, hnb]
        ring
      rintro (h1 | h1 | h1)
      · have : (q.den : 𝓞 ℚ) * a ∈ v.asIdeal := by
          rw [← hnb]; exact v.asIdeal.mul_mem_right b h1
        rcases v.isPrime.mem_or_mem this with h2 | h2
        · exact hcop ⟨h1, h2⟩
        · exact ha h2
      · have : (q.den : 𝓞 ℚ) * (a - b) ∈ v.asIdeal := by
          rw [← hdab]; exact v.asIdeal.mul_mem_right b h1
        rcases v.isPrime.mem_or_mem this with h2 | h2
        · refine hcop ⟨?_, h2⟩
          have hsum : ((q.num - q.den : ℤ) : 𝓞 ℚ) + (q.den : 𝓞 ℚ) = q.num := by
            push_cast; ring
          rw [← hsum]
          exact v.asIdeal.add_mem h1 h2
        · exact hab h2
      · have : (q.num : 𝓞 ℚ) * b ∈ v.asIdeal := by
          rw [hnb]; exact v.asIdeal.mul_mem_right a h1
        rcases v.isPrime.mem_or_mem this with h2 | h2
        · exact hcop ⟨h2, h1⟩
        · exact hb h2
    · intro h
      rw [not_or, not_or] at h
      obtain ⟨h1, h2, h3⟩ := h
      refine ⟨q.num, q.den, h1, h3, ?_, ?_⟩
      · push_cast at h2
        exact h2
      · rw [map_intCast, map_natCast, Rat.mul_den_eq_num]
  rw [MeetsBoundaryAt, key, not_not, intCast_mem_iff_natGenerator_dvd,
    intCast_mem_iff_natGenerator_dvd, natCast_mem_iff_natGenerator_dvd, hp.dvd_mul, hp.dvd_mul,
    or_assoc]

/-- `log p` if the prime `p` divides `m`, else `0`. -/
noncomputable def logIfDvd (m : ℕ) (p : {p : ℕ // p.Prime}) : ℝ :=
  if (p : ℕ) ∣ m then Real.log ((p : ℕ) : ℝ) else 0

/-- The sum of `log p` over the primes dividing `m ≠ 0` is the logarithm of the product of
these primes. -/
theorem finsum_logIfDvd (m : ℕ) (hm : m ≠ 0) :
    (∑ᶠ p : {p : ℕ // p.Prime}, logIfDvd m p) = Real.log ((∏ p ∈ m.primeFactors, p : ℕ) : ℝ) := by
  classical
  have hsupp : Function.support (logIfDvd m) ⊆ ↑(m.primeFactors.subtype Nat.Prime) := by
    intro p hp
    refine Finset.mem_coe.mpr (Finset.mem_subtype.mpr (Nat.mem_primeFactors.mpr ⟨p.2, ?_, hm⟩))
    by_contra h
    exact hp (by simp [logIfDvd, h])
  have hpt : ∀ p ∈ m.primeFactors.subtype Nat.Prime, logIfDvd m p = Real.log ((p : ℕ) : ℝ) :=
    fun p hp => by simp [logIfDvd, Nat.dvd_of_mem_primeFactors (Finset.mem_subtype.mp hp)]
  have hsub : ∑ p ∈ m.primeFactors.subtype Nat.Prime, Real.log ((p : ℕ) : ℝ) =
      ∑ k ∈ m.primeFactors, Real.log (k : ℝ) :=
    Finset.sum_subtype_of_mem (fun k : ℕ => Real.log (k : ℝ))
      (fun k hk => Nat.prime_of_mem_primeFactors hk)
  rw [finsum_eq_sum_of_support_subset _ hsupp, Finset.sum_congr rfl hpt, hsub, Nat.cast_prod,
    Real.log_prod]
  intro p hp
  exact_mod_cast (Nat.prime_of_mem_primeFactors hp).ne_zero

/-- The conductor of a rational number `q ∉ {0, 1}` is the product of the primes dividing
`|num q| · |num q - den q| · den q`. -/
theorem ratConductor_eq_prod_primeFactors (q : ℚ) (h0 : q ≠ 0) (h1 : q ≠ 1) :
    ratConductor q = ∏ p ∈ (q.num.natAbs * (q.num - q.den).natAbs * q.den).primeFactors, p := by
  have hn : q.num.natAbs ≠ 0 := Int.natAbs_ne_zero.mpr (Rat.num_ne_zero.mpr h0)
  have hnd : (q.num - q.den).natAbs ≠ 0 := by
    rw [← num_sub_one_eq_num_sub_den]
    exact Int.natAbs_ne_zero.mpr (Rat.num_ne_zero.mpr (sub_ne_zero.mpr h1))
  unfold ratConductor
  rw [num_sub_one_eq_num_sub_den, Nat.primeFactors_mul (Nat.mul_ne_zero hn hnd) q.den_nz,
    Nat.primeFactors_mul hn hnd]

/-- **The log-conductor of a rational point is `log (ratConductor q)`.** -/
theorem logCondNF_rat (q : ℚ) (h0 : q ≠ 0) (h1 : q ≠ 1) :
    logCondNF ℚ q = Real.log (ratConductor q) := by
  classical
  have hn : q.num.natAbs ≠ 0 := Int.natAbs_ne_zero.mpr (Rat.num_ne_zero.mpr h0)
  have hnd : (q.num - q.den).natAbs ≠ 0 := by
    rw [← num_sub_one_eq_num_sub_den]
    exact Int.natAbs_ne_zero.mpr (Rat.num_ne_zero.mpr (sub_ne_zero.mpr h1))
  have hm : q.num.natAbs * (q.num - q.den).natAbs * q.den ≠ 0 :=
    Nat.mul_ne_zero (Nat.mul_ne_zero hn hnd) q.den_nz
  have hpt : ∀ v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 ℚ),
      (if MeetsBoundaryAt ℚ v q then Real.log (Nat.card (𝓞 ℚ ⧸ v.asIdeal)) else 0) =
        logIfDvd (q.num.natAbs * (q.num - q.den).natAbs * q.den)
          (Rat.HeightOneSpectrum.primesEquiv v) := by
    intro v
    show _ = if Rat.HeightOneSpectrum.natGenerator v ∣
        q.num.natAbs * (q.num - q.den).natAbs * q.den then
      Real.log ((Rat.HeightOneSpectrum.natGenerator v : ℕ) : ℝ) else 0
    rw [card_quot_eq_natGenerator]
    by_cases h : Rat.HeightOneSpectrum.natGenerator v ∣
      q.num.natAbs * (q.num - q.den).natAbs * q.den
    · simp [(meetsBoundaryAt_rat_iff v q).mpr h, h]
    · simp [mt (meetsBoundaryAt_rat_iff v q).mp h, h]
  have hsum : (∑ᶠ v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 ℚ),
      if MeetsBoundaryAt ℚ v q then Real.log (Nat.card (𝓞 ℚ ⧸ v.asIdeal)) else 0) =
        Real.log (ratConductor q) := by
    rw [finsum_congr hpt, finsum_comp_equiv Rat.HeightOneSpectrum.primesEquiv
      (f := logIfDvd (q.num.natAbs * (q.num - q.den).natAbs * q.den)),
      ratConductor_eq_prod_primeFactors q h0 h1]
    exact finsum_logIfDvd _ hm
  unfold logCondNF
  rw [Module.finrank_self, Nat.cast_one, div_one]
  exact hsum

/-- The normalized height of a rational number is Mathlib's height on `ℚ`. -/
theorem heightNF_rat (q : ℚ) : heightNF ℚ q = Height.logHeight₁ q := by
  rw [heightNF, Module.finrank_self, Nat.cast_one, div_one]

/-- The log-different of `ℚ` is `0`: its discriminant is `1`. -/
theorem logDiffNF_rat : logDiffNF ℚ = 0 := by
  rw [logDiffNF_eq, Rat.numberField_discr]
  simp

end Rational

/-! ## Invariance of the log-conductor under isomorphisms -/

section Transport

variable {K L : Type*} [Field K] [NumberField K] [Field L] [NumberField L] (e : K ≃+* L)

omit [NumberField K] [NumberField L] in
/-- An isomorphism of number fields carries local representations `(a : b)` to local
representations, and back. -/
theorem reducesAwayFromBoundary_ringEquiv_iff (v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)) (y : K) :
    ReducesAwayFromBoundary L
        (HeightOneSpectrum.equivOfRingEquiv (RingOfIntegers.mapRingEquiv e) v) (e y) ↔
      ReducesAwayFromBoundary K v y := by
  have hc : ∀ z : 𝓞 K, algebraMap (𝓞 L) L (RingOfIntegers.mapRingEquiv e z) =
      e (algebraMap (𝓞 K) K z) := fun _ => rfl
  have hc' : ∀ z : 𝓞 L, algebraMap (𝓞 K) K ((RingOfIntegers.mapRingEquiv e).symm z) =
      e.symm (algebraMap (𝓞 L) L z) := fun _ => rfl
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨a, b, ha, hb, hab, h⟩
    refine ⟨(RingOfIntegers.mapRingEquiv e).symm a, (RingOfIntegers.mapRingEquiv e).symm b,
      ha, hb, ?_, ?_⟩
    · rw [← map_sub]; exact hab
    · rw [hc', hc', ← h, map_mul, RingEquiv.symm_apply_apply]
  · rintro ⟨a, b, ha, hb, hab, h⟩
    refine ⟨RingOfIntegers.mapRingEquiv e a, RingOfIntegers.mapRingEquiv e b, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
    · show (RingOfIntegers.mapRingEquiv e).symm (RingOfIntegers.mapRingEquiv e a) ∉ v.asIdeal
      rwa [RingEquiv.symm_apply_apply]
    · show (RingOfIntegers.mapRingEquiv e).symm (RingOfIntegers.mapRingEquiv e b) ∉ v.asIdeal
      rwa [RingEquiv.symm_apply_apply]
    · show (RingOfIntegers.mapRingEquiv e).symm
        (RingOfIntegers.mapRingEquiv e a - RingOfIntegers.mapRingEquiv e b) ∉ v.asIdeal
      rwa [← map_sub, RingEquiv.symm_apply_apply]
    · rw [hc, hc, ← map_mul, h]

omit [NumberField K] [NumberField L] in
/-- The residue fields at corresponding primes have the same cardinality. -/
theorem card_quot_equivOfRingEquiv (v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 K)) :
    Nat.card (𝓞 L ⧸
        (HeightOneSpectrum.equivOfRingEquiv (RingOfIntegers.mapRingEquiv e) v).asIdeal) =
      Nat.card (𝓞 K ⧸ v.asIdeal) :=
  (Nat.card_congr (Ideal.quotientEquiv v.asIdeal
    (HeightOneSpectrum.equivOfRingEquiv (RingOfIntegers.mapRingEquiv e) v).asIdeal
    (RingOfIntegers.mapRingEquiv e) (Ideal.comap_symm _)).toEquiv).symm

open Classical in
/-- **The log-conductor is invariant under isomorphisms of number fields.** -/
theorem logCondNF_ringEquiv (y : K) : logCondNF L (e y) = logCondNF K y := by
  unfold logCondNF
  rw [← e.toRatAlgEquiv.toLinearEquiv.finrank_eq,
    ← finsum_comp_equiv (HeightOneSpectrum.equivOfRingEquiv (RingOfIntegers.mapRingEquiv e))]
  congr 1
  refine finsum_congr fun v => ?_
  simp only [MeetsBoundaryAt, reducesAwayFromBoundary_ringEquiv_iff, card_quot_equivOfRingEquiv]
  by_cases h : ReducesAwayFromBoundary K v y <;> simp [h]

end Transport

/-! ## Degree one and the abc conjecture -/

/-- The degree one case implies the statement on rational points, by taking `F = ℚ`. -/
theorem rational_of_degreeAtMostOne (h : VojtaLineMinusThreePointsDegreeAtMost 1) :
    VojtaLineMinusThreePointsRational := by
  intro ε hε
  obtain ⟨C, hC⟩ := h ε hε
  refine ⟨C, fun q h0 h1 => ?_⟩
  have hq : IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {q} = ⊤ := eq_top_iff.mpr fun z _ => by
    simpa using IntermediateField.algebraMap_mem (IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {q}) z
  have := hC ℚ q (by exact hq) (Module.finrank_self ℚ).le h0 h1
  rwa [heightNF_rat, logDiffNF_rat, logCondNF_rat q h0 h1, zero_add] at this

/-- The statement on rational points implies the degree one case: a number field `F` of degree
one is isomorphic to `ℚ` through `algebraMap ℚ F`, the height of a rational number is the same
in `F` (`heightNF_algebraMap_rat`), and the log-different and the log-conductor are carried over
by the isomorphism. -/
theorem degreeAtMostOne_of_rational (h : VojtaLineMinusThreePointsRational) :
    VojtaLineMinusThreePointsDegreeAtMost 1 := by
  intro ε hε
  obtain ⟨C, hC⟩ := h ε hε
  refine ⟨C, ?_⟩
  intro F _ _ x _ hdeg hx0 hx1
  have hF : Module.finrank ℚ F = 1 := le_antisymm hdeg Module.finrank_pos
  have hbij := Algebra.finrank_eq_one_iff_bijective_algebraMap.mp hF
  obtain ⟨q, rfl⟩ := hbij.2 x
  have hq0 : q ≠ 0 := by rintro rfl; exact hx0 (map_zero _)
  have hq1 : q ≠ 1 := by rintro rfl; exact hx1 (map_one _)
  have hcond : logCondNF F (algebraMap ℚ F q) = Real.log (ratConductor q) := by
    rw [show algebraMap ℚ F q = RingEquiv.ofBijective (algebraMap ℚ F) hbij q from rfl,
      logCondNF_ringEquiv, logCondNF_rat q hq0 hq1]
  have hdiff : logDiffNF F = 0 := by
    rw [logDiffNF_eq, ← discr_eq_discr_of_ringEquiv (K := ℚ)
      (RingEquiv.ofBijective (algebraMap ℚ F) hbij), Rat.numberField_discr]
    simp
  rw [heightNF_algebraMap_rat, hdiff, hcond, zero_add]
  exact hC q hq0 hq1

/-- **The degree one case is equivalent to the statement on rational points.** -/
theorem degreeAtMostOne_iff_rational :
    VojtaLineMinusThreePointsDegreeAtMost 1 ↔ VojtaLineMinusThreePointsRational :=
  ⟨rational_of_degreeAtMostOne, degreeAtMostOne_of_rational⟩

/-- **The degree one case is equivalent to the abc conjecture.** Neither side is proved here. -/
theorem degreeAtMostOne_iff_ABC :
    VojtaLineMinusThreePointsDegreeAtMost 1 ↔ Challenge.ABC :=
  degreeAtMostOne_iff_rational.trans vojta_iff_ABC

/-- The statement for points of degree at most `d` implies the statement for degree at most
`d'` when `d' ≤ d`: the same constant works. -/
theorem degreeAtMost_mono {d d' : ℕ} (hd : d' ≤ d) (h : VojtaLineMinusThreePointsDegreeAtMost d) :
    VojtaLineMinusThreePointsDegreeAtMost d' := by
  intro ε hε
  obtain ⟨C, hC⟩ := h ε hε
  exact ⟨C, fun F _ _ x hx hdeg => hC F x hx (hdeg.trans hd)⟩

/-- **For every `d ≥ 1`, the statement for points of degree at most `d` implies the abc
conjecture.** For `d = 0` the statement is vacuous: no number field has degree `0`. -/
theorem abc_of_degreeAtMost {d : ℕ} (hd : 1 ≤ d) (h : VojtaLineMinusThreePointsDegreeAtMost d) :
    Challenge.ABC :=
  degreeAtMostOne_iff_ABC.mp (degreeAtMost_mono hd h)

/-- **The bounded degree statement implies the abc conjecture.** Neither is proved here. -/
theorem abc_of_boundedDegree (h : VojtaLineMinusThreePointsBoundedDegree) : Challenge.ABC :=
  degreeAtMostOne_iff_ABC.mp (h 1 le_rfl)

/-! ## A point of degree two -/

section Example

/- The example is stated for every number field `K` that is a third cyclotomic extension of `ℚ`,
that is, `K ≅ ℚ(ζ₃) = ℚ(√-3)`; Mathlib's `CyclotomicField 3 ℚ` is one. -/
variable (K : Type*) [Field K] [NumberField K] [IsCyclotomicExtension {3} ℚ K]

/-- The point `-ζ₃` of `ℚ(ζ₃)`, a primitive sixth root of unity, with `ζ₃` Mathlib's chosen
primitive cube root of unity `IsCyclotomicExtension.zeta 3 ℚ K`. -/
noncomputable def sixthRoot : K :=
  -IsCyclotomicExtension.zeta 3 ℚ K

/-- `ℚ(ζ₃)` has degree `2`. -/
theorem finrank_cyclotomicThree : Module.finrank ℚ K = 2 := by
  rw [IsCyclotomicExtension.finrank (n := 3) K
    (Polynomial.cyclotomic.irreducible_rat (by norm_num)), Nat.totient_prime Nat.prime_three]

theorem sixthRoot_ne_zero : sixthRoot K ≠ 0 := by
  have hζ := IsCyclotomicExtension.zeta_spec 3 ℚ K
  unfold sixthRoot
  exact neg_ne_zero.mpr (hζ.ne_zero (by norm_num))

theorem sixthRoot_ne_one : sixthRoot K ≠ 1 := by
  have hζ := IsCyclotomicExtension.zeta_spec 3 ℚ K
  unfold sixthRoot
  intro h
  have hz : IsCyclotomicExtension.zeta 3 ℚ K = -1 := by
    rw [← neg_neg (IsCyclotomicExtension.zeta 3 ℚ K), h]
  have h2 : IsCyclotomicExtension.zeta 3 ℚ K ^ 2 = 1 := by
    rw [hz]; norm_num
  have := hζ.dvd_of_pow_eq_one 2 h2
  norm_num at this

/-- `-ζ₃` generates `ℚ(ζ₃)`. -/
theorem adjoin_sixthRoot_eq_top : IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {sixthRoot K} = ⊤ := by
  have hζ := IsCyclotomicExtension.zeta_spec 3 ℚ K
  set z := IsCyclotomicExtension.zeta 3 ℚ K
  have hz : IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {z} = ⊤ := by
    apply IntermediateField.toSubalgebra_injective
    rw [IntermediateField.adjoin_simple_toSubalgebra_of_isAlgebraic
      (Algebra.IsAlgebraic.isAlgebraic z), IntermediateField.top_toSubalgebra]
    exact IsCyclotomicExtension.adjoin_primitive_root_eq_top hζ
  rw [← hz, show sixthRoot K = -z from rfl]
  refine le_antisymm (IntermediateField.adjoin_simple_le_iff.mpr ?_)
    (IntermediateField.adjoin_simple_le_iff.mpr ?_)
  · exact neg_mem (IntermediateField.subset_adjoin ℚ {z} (Set.mem_singleton z))
  · simpa using neg_mem (IntermediateField.subset_adjoin ℚ {-z} (Set.mem_singleton (-z)))

/-- **The height of `-ζ₃` is `0`**: it is a root of unity. -/
theorem heightNF_sixthRoot : heightNF K (sixthRoot K) = 0 := by
  have hζ := IsCyclotomicExtension.zeta_spec 3 ℚ K
  have h6 : sixthRoot K ^ 6 = 1 := by
    have : sixthRoot K ^ 6 = (IsCyclotomicExtension.zeta 3 ℚ K ^ 3) ^ 2 := by
      unfold sixthRoot; ring
    rw [this, hζ.pow_eq_one, one_pow]
  have := Height.logHeight₁_pow (sixthRoot K) 6
  rw [h6, Height.logHeight₁_one] at this
  have h0 : Height.logHeight₁ (sixthRoot K) = 0 := by
    norm_num at this
    linarith
  rw [heightNF, h0, zero_div]

/-- **The log-different of `ℚ(ζ₃)` is `(1/2) log 3`**: its discriminant is `-3`
(`IsCyclotomicExtension.Rat.discr_prime`). -/
theorem logDiffNF_cyclotomicThree : logDiffNF K = Real.log 3 / 2 := by
  rw [logDiffNF_eq, IsCyclotomicExtension.Rat.discr_prime 3 K, finrank_cyclotomicThree]
  norm_num

/-- **The log-conductor of `-ζ₃` is `0`**: `x = -ζ₃` and `x - 1 = ζ₃²` are units, so `x` meets
`{0, 1, ∞}` at no prime. -/
theorem logCondNF_sixthRoot : logCondNF K (sixthRoot K) = 0 := by
  have hζ := IsCyclotomicExtension.zeta_spec 3 ℚ K
  have hu : IsPrimitiveRoot hζ.toInteger 3 := hζ.toInteger_isPrimitiveRoot
  have hunit : IsUnit hζ.toInteger := hu.isUnit (by norm_num)
  have hrel : hζ.toInteger ^ 2 + hζ.toInteger + 1 = 0 := by
    have h3 : hζ.toInteger ^ 3 = 1 := hu.pow_eq_one
    have hne : hζ.toInteger ≠ 1 := hu.ne_one (by norm_num)
    have hprod : (hζ.toInteger - 1) * (hζ.toInteger ^ 2 + hζ.toInteger + 1) = 0 := by
      rw [show (hζ.toInteger - 1) * (hζ.toInteger ^ 2 + hζ.toInteger + 1) =
        hζ.toInteger ^ 3 - 1 by ring, h3, sub_self]
    exact (mul_eq_zero.mp hprod).resolve_left (sub_ne_zero.mpr hne)
  unfold logCondNF
  rw [finsum_eq_zero_of_forall_eq_zero, zero_div]
  intro v
  have hnot : ∀ w : 𝓞 K, IsUnit w → w ∉ v.asIdeal :=
    fun w hw hmem => v.isPrime.ne_top (Ideal.eq_top_of_isUnit_mem _ hmem hw)
  have hr : ReducesAwayFromBoundary K v (sixthRoot K) := by
    refine ⟨-hζ.toInteger, 1, hnot _ hunit.neg, hnot _ isUnit_one, ?_, ?_⟩
    · have : -hζ.toInteger - 1 = hζ.toInteger ^ 2 := by linear_combination -hrel
      rw [this]
      exact hnot _ (hunit.pow 2)
    · rw [map_one, mul_one, map_neg, ← RingOfIntegers.coe_eq_algebraMap]
      simp only [sixthRoot, neg_inj]
      exact hζ.coe_toInteger.symm
  simp [MeetsBoundaryAt, hr]

/-- **A concrete point of degree two.** In Mathlib's `CyclotomicField 3 ℚ`, of degree `2` and
log-different `(1/2) log 3`, the point `-ζ₃` generates the field, lies outside `{0, 1}`, and has
height `0` and log-conductor `0`. -/
theorem exists_point_cyclotomicFieldThree :
    Module.finrank ℚ (CyclotomicField 3 ℚ) = 2 ∧
      logDiffNF (CyclotomicField 3 ℚ) = Real.log 3 / 2 ∧
      ∃ x : CyclotomicField 3 ℚ, IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {x} = ⊤ ∧ x ≠ 0 ∧ x ≠ 1 ∧
        heightNF (CyclotomicField 3 ℚ) x = 0 ∧ logCondNF (CyclotomicField 3 ℚ) x = 0 := by
  have : IsCyclotomicExtension {3} ℚ (CyclotomicField 3 ℚ) :=
    CyclotomicField.isCyclotomicExtension 3 ℚ
  exact ⟨finrank_cyclotomicThree _, logDiffNF_cyclotomicThree _, sixthRoot _,
    adjoin_sixthRoot_eq_top _, sixthRoot_ne_zero _, sixthRoot_ne_one _, heightNF_sixthRoot _,
    logCondNF_sixthRoot _⟩

end Example

end IUT.VojtaNumberField
